DocAI — third-party data attribution
=====================================

The receipt images and ground-truth labels under data/cord_receipts/ are derived from:

    CORD: A Consolidated Receipt Dataset for Post-OCR Parsing (CORD-v2)
    https://huggingface.co/datasets/naver-clova-ix/cord-v2
    License: CC-BY-4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)
    Park et al., "CORD: A Consolidated Receipt Dataset for Post-OCR Parsing",
    Document Intelligence Workshop at NeurIPS 2019.

DocAI downloads a small sample of real CORD receipt images and their real annotated
fields (line items, subtotal, tax, total) and flattens each into DocAI's receipt schema
for use by the evaluation pipeline (ml/pipelines/evaluation.py). Attribution is retained
in accordance with CC-BY-4.0. DocAI's own source code is under the MIT License (see
LICENSE).

Regenerate the sample with: python data/download_cord.py
